+### Planning a sprint
+
+« Plan » on a sprint opens the backlog and the sprint side by side.
+
+- **Capacity gauge**: the sprint's points against the velocity of the last 3 closed sprints, with their bars beside it. A team that is short this sprint sets its availability in %. A first sprint, with no history yet, aims at 20 points. Points only, never a duration.
+- **Moving tasks**: drag them from one side to the other (ticked tasks go together), or press → / ← on a title; « Undo » or Ctrl+Z takes the last move back. The backlog has quick filters (urgent, bugs, not estimated), and « Estimate » runs Smart Estimation on a task without points.
+- **On the sprint side**, a task carried over from the previous sprint says so, and a task waiting on one left in the backlog shows « Waits on… » with « Add it too ». A planned sprint starts from the view.
+- **Propose the sprint** (on the sprint banner and in the planning view): the rules rank the backlog (priority, bugs, what a task unblocks, the sprint goal, age), then the selected provider's model composes the sprint up to its capacity and gives a reason for each task, in the app's language. A task's blockers come in first, and the best tasks that don't fit are shown below the line. Four variants: Balanced, More careful (80 % of the capacity), Bugs first, Around the goal. When the sprint has no goal, one is suggested. Nothing moves until « Add N cards », which can be undone. Without a model, the rules propose on their own.
+- **Privacy**: the model only reads a task's title, the start of its description, its priority, type, points, labels and dependencies, never who works on it.
+
+Design: [kanban-sprints.md](https://github.com/krovomi/WorkPilot-AI/blob/develop/docs/architecture/kanban-sprints.md), [sprint-proposal.md](https://github.com/krovomi/WorkPilot-AI/blob/develop/docs/architecture/sprint-proposal.md).
+
+![Propose the sprint: the cards offered in dashed violet with their reason, the capacity line and what falls below it](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/krovomi/WorkPilot-AI/develop/.github/assets/screenshots/sprint-proposal.png)
+
 ### Working fast on the board
 
 - **Card colours**: each card takes the colour of its type (14 types in 5 families: feature, bug fix, refactoring, security…), read from its kind, category, severity and origin, nothing to fill in; a preview opens after 700 ms on hover. A finished card shows the agents' time, tokens and cost, who created it and who started it.
